From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH] rfkill: set WLAN platform driver data

rfkill_wlan_remove() retrieves its state with platform_get_drvdata(), but the
probe path never stores the allocated state on the platform device. Unbinding
wlan-platdata therefore passes NULL to wake_lock_destroy() and crashes during
device removal. Store the state when probe succeeds.

---
 net/rfkill/rfkill-wlan.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/net/rfkill/rfkill-wlan.c b/net/rfkill/rfkill-wlan.c
index 8b2f57c9e2a1..9d21cbf70000 100644
--- a/net/rfkill/rfkill-wlan.c
+++ b/net/rfkill/rfkill-wlan.c
@@ -810,5 +810,6 @@ static int rfkill_wlan_probe(struct platform_device *pdev) {
 	fb_register_client(&rfkill_wlan_fb_notifier);
 
+	platform_set_drvdata(pdev, rfkill);
 	LOG("Exit %s\n", __func__);
 
 	return 0;
-- 
2.43.0
